y; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-e1d22f, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-e1d22f)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-e1d22f, pid=20802, exit=1)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-e1d22f queued successor RUN-260831-a3b6c1 (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): spawned agent exited with code 1\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-a3b6c1)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=-1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-a3b6c1, pid=34981, exit=-1)\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=claude/claude-opus-5/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:cc7e0eb08c9f43b208cba223816e0e602248ca4021a13ced3c4b5b3f3ddae606 rationale="Consciously choosing rank-2: the rank-1 codex pair was blocked four consecutive times by the provider content filter on this reviewers adversarial probes, so Opus is the only viable path and additionally gives cross-provider review independence."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (run=RUN-260831-a35299, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run RUN-260831-a3b6c1 cancelled by operator; operator action required; reason: Fourth provider content-filter block on this reviewer; switching the reviewer role to Opus per owner authorization.\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (run=RUN-260831-a35299)\nCR revision 7 review: CHANGES REQUESTED. One blocking attestation-integrity defect, one unsupported README claim, one gate-stall finding. F1 (blocking): Session Record 1.0.0 name is validated only by a bare requireString, so it carries no constraint at all. SPEC 5.1 declares name as the Section 2.3 grammar, which SPEC 2.1 defines as 1-64 characters matching [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}. The reviewer drove both public entries and both CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity attested names containing a newline, a tab, ../../etc/passwd, $(rm -rf /), 1024 characters, 65 characters, a space, a leading hyphen and non-ASCII text. Every other declared member of the 5.1 table IS enforced; name is the single dropped one, and it is dropped identically in TASK-260830-8x76g1_constraint-enumeration.md, whose Session Record paragraph never mentions it. The systematic-enumeration DoD item is therefore not met for the one schema whose complete shape this candidate claims to own. F2: README states the three accepted schemas complete shapes are validated here; given F1 that claim does not reproduce, recurring the rev3 finding. F3: validateManifestEntries compares each entry path against every earlier one with strings.EqualFold; a contract-valid 65536-entry workspace_tree manifest of 3211786 bytes, inside the 5242880-byte identity cap, spends 6.61s in CalculateObjectIdentity (2000/17ms, 8000/162ms, 20000/875ms) - CPU amplification on peer-supplied input; entries are already strictly sorted and unique so a lowercased set makes it linear. WHAT IS SOLID, do not rework: the totality gate is real (removing one register row panics at init with missing immutable-object shape validator for urn:ax:schema:migration-checkpoint@1.0.0); the fuzz-wiring gate is real and AST-derived (an unwired FuzzReviewMutantUnwiredTarget fails TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget); four NARROWING mutants are each killed by a named test (byte-vs-character bounds, BlobChunk index equality, extensions reverse-DNS grammar, symlink target bound); the byte-vs-character audit is correct in BOTH directions - argv/env_literals/task_element_id are declared in BYTES and implemented in bytes, media_type/symlink target/logical_id/goal_id/repository_identity/tree_identity/remote name are declared in CHARACTERS and accept multibyte values exactly at the bound; Sections 10.2-10.4 member sets, kind invariants, sparse pairing, submodule depth/count/acyclicity, gitlink binding and TM-GIT-N2 all match the pinned tables; accepted-leaf scalar content is byte-identical to the checkpoint tarball. Reviewer re-ran build, vet, go test ./... (8 packages ok), tracecheck -section 17.3 (assigned_scopes=1) and all four fuzz targets at 100x - all exit 0; race/cover/gofmt/cataloggen/cross-builds accepted from the rev7 validation log. REWORK METHOD: do not add only a name regex. Five rounds have each fixed exactly the named field and been defeated by the next unenumerated one. Apply the structural fix at the FIELD level the way it was applied at the registry level: the enumeration artifact must carry one row per declared member of every completely-validated schema, each naming its enforcing call site, with an explicit quoted row for members that genuinely carry no constraint beyond their type, preferably derived from the requireExactMembers argument lists so artifact and code cannot drift. Then fix F2 and F3. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_review-verdict-rev7.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_review-evidence-rev7.tar.gz. Working tree verified byte-identical to candidate tree 2101a33011a27c98903679163545a7a778027b07 before and after every probe and mutant.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260831-a35299, pid=35903, exit=0)\nCR revision 7 reviewed by claude/opus after the codex reviewer was blocked four consecutive times by the provider content filter. The switch paid off immediately: F3 is a measured CPU-amplification defect no earlier round found. validateManifestEntries compares each path against every earlier one with strings.EqualFold, which is about 2.1e9 comparisons at the declared 65536-entry maximum. Measured: a well-formed 65536-entry workspace_tree manifest encodes to 3211786 bytes, inside the 5242880 identity cap, and CalculateObjectIdentity spends 6.61 seconds on it; scaling is quadratic at 17ms, 162ms and 875ms for 2000, 8000 and 20000 entries. Transfer Manifests arrive from peers over Mesh RPC, so this is CPU amplification on untrusted input at a validation gate. Entries are already required strictly sorted and unique, so a lowercased-path set makes it linear with no loss of coverage. F1 is narrower than earlier rounds and confirms the totality instruction worked: every declared member of the Session Record table is enforced except name, which uses a bare requireString while Section 5.1 defers to the Section 2.3 and 2.1 grammar. The reviewer extends the structural remedy from the registry level to the FIELD level and that instruction is adopted verbatim: produce a per-member enumeration derived from the requireExactMembers argument lists so a dropped constraint shows up as a missing row instead of a silent omission. F2 is a README completeness claim that does not reproduce.\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:97a03f5c6378c00c3c16903d1bd83dfac31eeecb8d234a0b749b016e8ac47eb6 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: close a measured CPU-amplification vector on untrusted input and make the constraint enumeration total at the member level rather than adding one more named field."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implemente