+# TASK-260830-8x76g1 — developer rework revision 8
+
+## Outcome
+
+CR revision 7 findings are addressed without changing the accepted scalar,
+catalog, cataloggen, or spec-pin leaf content.
+
+- `validateSessionRecordV1`, reached only through
+  `prepareObjectIdentity -> validateImmutableObjectShape`, now enforces the
+  Section 2.1/5.1 Session Record name term
+  `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}`. A 64-character name is accepted; 65
+  characters, a leading hyphen, a space, a control character, and non-ASCII
+  text are refused through both `CalculateObjectIdentity` and
+  `VerifyObjectIdentity`.
+- `validateManifestEntries` now performs destination-case collision detection
+  with an O(total path characters) map. `simpleFoldKey` canonicalizes Unicode
+  simple-fold orbits, preserving the previous `strings.EqualFold` collision
+  classes rather than narrowing the gate to ASCII or lowercase-only behavior.
+- `TestTransferManifestMaximumEntryGateIsLinear` drives
+  `CalculateObjectIdentity` with 65,536 valid directory entries inside the
+  5,242,880-byte input cap. The final run took 0.30s, below the 2s guard.
+- `TestConstraintEnumerationMatchesRequireExactMembers` derives 167 member
+  rows from every production `requireExactMembers` call in the scoped complete
+  validators. It requires one artifact row per member, rejects an undocumented
+  new shape call, and verifies each row names its production enforcing call
+  site. The committed artifact also enumerates reachable tagged, ordering,
+  recursive, cross-field, and external-boundary rules without claiming that
+  referenced Blob, child-manifest, Git, or filesystem evidence is locally
+  proven.
+- `FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal` includes a committed malformed Session name
+  seed and remains invoked by the configured fixed `100x`, one-worker gate.
+- README capability prose now names the Session name grammar, the AST-bound
+  per-member inventory, and the linear maximum-entry regression. It retains
+  the existing explicit non-claims for migration publication, atomic reference
+  advancement, filesystem/materialization checks, and runtime capabilities.
+
+## Negative evidence
+
+All expected-red commands below were run directly and truthfully returned
+non-zero:
+
+| Candidate / mutation | Command | Exit | Evidence |
+| --- | --- | ---: | --- |
+| Exact CR rev7 candidate | `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run '^TestReviewSessionNameGrammarGate$' -count=1 -v` | 1 | `CalculateObjectIdentity` attested `-payments` instead of refusing it. |
+| Exact CR rev7 candidate | `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run '^TestTransferManifestMaximumEntryGateIsLinear$' -count=1 -v` | 1 | 65,536-entry calculation took 6.575s, over the 2s guard. |
+| Revision 8 inventory with only `Session Record 1.0.0.name` row removed | `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run '^TestConstraintEnumerationMatchesRequireExactMembers$' -count=1 -v` | 1 | Exact failure: `missing artifact row Session Record 1.0.0.name`. |
+
+The original revision 8 race attempt also returned exit 1 because wall-clock
+instrumentation made the performance test take 2.872s; it reported no data
+race. The timing-only test was moved to a `!race` test file. Functional
+collision/refusal tests remain in the race suite, whose final run returned 0.
+
+## Final validation
+
+Every configured command was rerun as a standalone foreground process on the
+final bytes. No command was piped through `tee`; pipeline status was preserved
+for the configured JSON gate.
+
+| Gate | Exit |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Go format check | 0 |
+| `go build ./...` | 0 |
+| `go vet ./...` | 0 |
+| `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 0 |
+| `go test ./... -race -count=1` | 0 |
+| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 |
+| Four configured fuzz targets, each `-fuzztime=100x -parallel=1` | 0 each |
+| Full `tracecheck` | 0 |
+| `tracecheck -section 17.3` | 0 (`assigned_scopes=1`) |
+| Catalog generation check | 0 |
+| Linux amd64 build | 0 |
+| Windows amd64 build | 0 |
+| Tracked JSON parse gate | 0 |
+| `task-board validate` | 0 |
+| `git diff --check` | 0 |
+
+Coverage in the final run: canonicaljson 80.8%, scalar 90.1%, catalog 97.6%,
+cataloggen 83.9%, specpin 85.1%, traceability 85.0%, and tracecheck 87.5%.
+`task-board validate` still prints 262 inherited `MISSING_ACTIVITY`
+diagnostics while returning exit 0; the current task is not listed.
+
+The operation is deterministic and read-only. It mutates no durable runtime
+state, so crash/idempotency evidence is not applicable.
+
+## Source binding
+
+- Pinned SPEC clone: commit
+  `28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`; SPEC.md SHA-256
+  `562546d240f0fa3e71b47e6359a002f9892c0efd97e19eb55917527552ac484a`.
+- Accepted-leaves archive SHA-256:
+  `9ae5e624addc7d954c391d96cab7c9f7aac3e6bcee58c76dd0cc95533d0eac9c`.
+  Go module files, specpin, catalog, cataloggen, and the accepted scalar core
+  were compared byte-for-byte and remain exact.
+- Carryforward archive SHA-256:
+  `df8d8fa712e0ce85bde4776dc1f83cef9d373593e76fd1145ce9d85b593ce4ee`.
+  It was inspected as the recovery basis; the working candidate already
+  contained later reviewed revisions, so it was not destructively overlaid.
+- Revision 8 was diff-reviewed against exact CR revision 7 candidate tree
+  `2101a33011a27c98903679163545a7a778027b07`, not merely against the older Story
+  base.
